# Entrypoints and dreaming — 2026-11-11
#
# The owner asked to review more of the site consumer's direction and consider the snippet patterns and file structures that could clarify entrypoints into well-considered domains of expression; the same evening they named the dreaming architecture, taste-based refinements to the runtime and parsers, and implementing plans.
# Read only; the counts are from the site consumer's .spw outside _workbench and gen, read in place through this repo's parser.

#>journal_2026_11_11_entrypoints_and_dreaming
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-11"
 kind: #observation
 base: "the site consumer's working tree of the same evening, mounted at 9ef3d223, with another session's edits uncommitted; this repo at 9ef3d223 plus the reading-drift slices"
 method: "read the consumer's canon index, snippets index, the dreamable-codebases and workbench-interaction caches, its sleep cycle's header, and its capability and corpus asks; ran findRhymes over its 490 surfaces; counted register tags and header facts with grep"
 limits: "the bidirectional-parsing, runtime-library and design-improvements caches were not read; the snippet generator's classifier was not read; nothing in the consumer was run or written"
}

^["dreaming"]{
 reading: "the owner's dreaming architecture is read here as the consumer's sense sleep: a night re-runs read-only probes, compares sorted, position-free digests, replays the day's words against cold questions, proposes retirements, babbles one-slot turns that land on another page's line, and counts what the last note paid. That reading is this entry's, not the owner's"
 workbench_side: "canonical/dream-schedule.ts models beat-scheduled, measure-only phases with CLI hints nothing runs (lukewarm-backlog ?[dream_orphan], curiosity-mutation-ergonomics ?[reuse_dream]); the consumer's sleep is the working instance"
 lifts: "the consumer's asks map onto it: inquiry_loop (rank 1: a run kept as a receipt with a stable digest, ~#expect with a comparable slot, the verdict a reader's), turns_that_land (rank 9: one slot changed, kept only when the corpus already holds it, which is two rhyme instances one hole apart), seeded_mosey (rank 10: a deterministic walk along citations toward cold surfaces)"
 gate: "reading-drift is the night's question asked of a grammar change: what moved while no one looked, as a list, with the text hash saying whether the text or the reader moved"
}

^["snippets"]{
 handles: "@_: ~_ (a handle bound to a path) is written 5,125 times in 454 of 490 surfaces: every surface names its neighbours first, so the handle block is the corpus's real entry grammar"
 signature: "262 surfaces carry an expression = line, a one-line signature of what the surface is (expression = corpus[snippets]{shell.spw.instruction}<runnable>); it does for a surface what a plan card's gist and the story consumer's op container(place)@keeper do for a plan and a room"
 header_twice: "479 surfaces write #:operation and 314 write operation = ; 300 write both, one fact in two spellings"
 register_tags: "3,128 [reg=set] tags, 3,067 closing a [ ] frame, beside 3,209 #[ openers; 4,141 [reg=facet] tags, 4,135 after a closing }; the tag mostly restates what the opener already says"
 index_twice: "the root index binds about thirty handles and then lists most of them again in a dispatch facet"
 snippets_index: "the generated snippets index repeats a key inside one facet (one anchor's validation probes share a key) and files prose instructions under probe[shell], against its own falsification line; the parser here reads a repeated key in a facet without a word"
}

^["entrypoints"]{
 # Offers for the consumer and for this repo; none decided.
 signature_line: "a domain's index lists its members by their signature lines, generated, so a folder reads as a table of what each surface is, and spw ls or tree can print the line beside the path"
 one_spelling: "a header fact lives once, as the particle the parser already reads; a binding that repeats it is generated or dropped"
 derived_dispatch: "a dispatch facet that only renames handles is derivable from the handle block, so an index keeps one list"
 domain_card: "a domain folder opens like a plan: a card with a gist, first reads for a newcomer and for someone fluent, and the probes that say whether the domain still holds"
 dreamable_question: "?[q]{ ~#expect: guess  !probe{ command } } with an optional comparable slot is the snippet a night can test; a question with no guess measures and does not test"
 register_tag: "whether [reg=set] after #[ ] and [reg=facet] after .{ } carry anything the opener does not is a reading for interpretation-trials, not a format rule"
}
